  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In the 1950s, reports from the Air Force's criminal investigations office described photos of what looked like flying butane tanks, and David Grusch, a former Air Force intelligence officer, says these were the same kind of thing as the Tic Tac, the white oval object shaped like the mint that Navy pilots reported in recent years. He tells Michels that \"the tic tac of today was the flying butane tank photo of the 1950s,\" passing on what he was told about those old files. If so, the military has been seeing the same objects for some seventy years."
